-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Rust crate dependencies
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

trakktor builds on numerous Rust crates (declared in Cargo.toml, pinned in
Cargo.lock), predominantly under the MIT and/or Apache-2.0 licenses. Each crate
remains under its own license; Cargo.lock is the authoritative list of the
exact versions in use. Two of them are not MIT/Apache-2.0 and are called out
here: `clipper2-rust` (polygon offsetting for the OCR detector) is under the
Boost Software License 1.0, and `nalgebra`/`simba`, reached through
`imageproc`, are Apache-2.0 only rather than dual-licensed. When distributing compiled binaries, generate the full
set of dependency license texts with a tool such as `cargo about` or
`cargo bundle-licenses`.


